      "username": "Dje",
      "name": null,
      "created_at": "2026-02-23T21:08:06.025Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I’m experiencing the same issue. I’ve reported it as a bug on GitHub: <a href=\"https://github.com/frappe/erpnext/issues/52913\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">SQL Syntax Error in Financial Statements (v16.6.1): Missing space in 'andcoalesce' for user permission filters · Issue #52913 · frappe/erpnext · GitHub</a></p>\n<p>Workaround: Remove the Company User Permission for the affected user. As long as the user has the “Accounts Manager” role, they’ll still have full access to accounting reports and can edit accounts without restriction.</p>",
